ent", "Garrity's late skill-games fundraising has not moved the polling picture"], "rationale": "Every recent poll, including Republican-leaning ones, shows Shapiro ahead by double digits, and raters and markets unanimously treat the race as decided. Garrity's late fundraising surge tied to the skill games industry has not dented a lead built on incumbency in a state that leans only slightly Democratic.", "watch": "A major late scandal or a wave of Republican outside spending could narrow the margin, though the outcome would be unlikely to change.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Josh Shapiro enters the final week of his reelection bid with a commanding position. Polls since August have shown him leading Republican Stacy Garrity by roughly 16 to 30 points, including surveys from Quinnipiac, Siena, and Franklin & Marshall, and even Republican-leaning pollsters put him ahead by double digits. Every major race rating, from Cook to Sabato, places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and betting markets give Shapiro a 97 to 99 percent chance of winning.\n\nGarrity's campaign drew attention late with a surge of donations tied to the skill games industry, but there is little evidence the money has changed the race's trajectory. Pennsylvania's near-even partisan lean is outweighed by Shapiro's incumbency and his standing with voters. The realistic question is the size of the margin, not the winner, with third-party candidate Ken Krawchuk drawing only minor support.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "